📜 Privacy Policy – Flippy Bird

Effective Date: 14/09/2025 (last updated 30/10/2026)

Flippy Bird ("the Game", "we", "our", "us") respects your privacy and is committed to protecting your personal information. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and safeguard information when you use our mobile game.

1. Information We Collect

When you use Flippy Bird, we may collect the following information:

Account Information: When you sign in with Google (Firebase Authentication), your email address, display name and a Firebase user ID, used for authentication and leaderboard features.

Gameplay Data: Your highest scores for different game modes, stored in Firebase to display in leaderboards.

Device Information: General device information (such as device model, operating system version, and country) collected by analytics or advertising services.

Advertising Data: We use Google AdMob to serve ads, which may collect data such as device identifiers, cookies, and usage information for personalized or non-personalized ads.

2. How We Use Information

We use the collected information to:

Authenticate your account with Google Play Games.

Store and update your best scores in Firebase leaderboards.

Display global leaderboards and rankings.

Improve gameplay experience and fix bugs.

Show ads to support free access to the Game.

3. Sharing of Information

We do not sell or rent your personal data. We only share limited information with:

Google Play Games Services for login and leaderboard features.

Firebase for securely storing and updating scores.

Google AdMob for serving advertisements.

These third-party services may collect and process data according to their own privacy policies.

4. User Choices

If you do not log in with Google Play Games, you will not have access to the leaderboards.

You can disable personalized ads through your device settings.

You may request deletion of your leaderboard data by contacting us.

Data processed by third-party SDKs (as declared in Google Play Data safety)

This section lists, for Flippy Bird (Tap To Fly), the data processed by the third-party SDKs included in the app. It matches the Data safety form of the app on Google Play.

- Google AdMob (advertising): collects and shares with Google the advertising ID / app set ID and other device identifiers, an approximate location derived from your IP address, ad interactions (impressions, clicks) and diagnostics (such as app launches and performance). Purposes: advertising, ad measurement and analytics, and fraud prevention and security. We do not receive your name or contact details from AdMob.
- Firebase Analytics (Google): app interactions (events and screens viewed), the Firebase installation ID / device identifiers, and basic device and app information. Purposes: analytics and app functionality.
- Firebase Crashlytics (Google): crash logs and diagnostics (stack trace, device model, Android and app version, a random installation ID). Purposes: analytics and app stability.
- Firebase Cloud Messaging (Google): a push token / Firebase installation ID, used to deliver notifications. Purpose: app functionality.
- Account data (Firebase Authentication with Google Sign-In): email address, display name and user ID. Purposes: app functionality and account management.
- Scores and progress (Cloud Firestore): your best scores per game mode, tied to your user ID, to show the leaderboards. Purpose: app functionality.

Consent: where required (European Economic Area, United Kingdom, Switzerland) the app asks for your consent through Google's User Messaging Platform (UMP) before showing ads.
Ad choices: you can reset or delete your advertising ID and opt out of ads personalisation in Android Settings > Google > Ads.
Security: data sent to these services travels encrypted in transit (HTTPS/TLS).
Data deletion: to ask for the deletion of data linked to you, use https://tlldevelopers.com/taptofly-delete-account.html or write to tll.developers.apps@gmail.com.

5. Children’s Privacy

Flippy Bird is not directed at children under 13. If you are under 13, please do not use the Game without parental consent.

6. Data Security

We take reasonable measures to protect your information from unauthorized access, alteration, or disclosure. However, no system is 100% secure.

7. Changes to This Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted within the Game or app store listing with a new “Effective Date.”

